@startuml direct-rialto-notification-sequence
title direct-rialto: notifications from the sink back into PrivateInstanceAAMP

participant "Rialto event thread" as RT
participant AampRialtoPlayer as ARP
participant "GLib main loop\n(progress / MonitorAV ticks)" as GL
participant PrivateInstanceAAMPNotifiable as NOT
participant "AAMP scheduler thread" as SCH
participant PrivateInstanceAAMP as CORE
participant "Injector thread" as INJ
participant AampRialtoMonitorAV as MAV

== Rialto state change -> async notification ==
RT -> ARP : OnPlaybackState(PLAYING)
ARP -> ARP : stateMachine.onPlaybackStarted()
alt first PLAYING of the session
	ARP -> NOT : LogFirstFrame(), LogTuneComplete()
	ARP -> NOT : NotifyFirstBufferProcessed(videoRect)
	ARP -> NOT : NotifyFirstFrameReceived(ccHandle)
	ARP -> NOT : NotifyFirstVideoFrameDisplayed()
else later PLAYING while core state is SEEKING
	ARP -> NOT : GetState()  (synchronous query)
	NOT -> CORE : GetState()
	ARP -> NOT : NotifyFirstBufferProcessed / NotifyFirstFrameReceived /\nNotifyFirstVideoFrameDisplayed
else other PLAYING (resume from pause)
	ARP -> NOT : NotifyFirstBufferProcessed / NotifyFirstFrameReceived
end
NOT -> SCH : ScheduleAsyncTask(name, lambda)\n(returns immediately)
SCH -> CORE : NotifyFirstFrameReceived() etc.\n(state PLAYING, tuned event, InitializeCC)
ARP -> ARP : StartProgressTimer(); MonitorAV.start()

== Periodic progress ==
GL -> ARP : OnProgressTimerTick()
ARP -> NOT : MonitorProgress(false, false)
NOT -> SCH : ScheduleAsyncTask
SCH -> CORE : MonitorProgress() -> progress event

== Errors and end of stream ==
RT -> ARP : OnPlaybackState(FAILURE / END_OF_STREAM)\nOnPlaybackError(...)\nOnBufferUnderflow(...)
ARP -> NOT : NotifyPlaybackError(failure, text, retry)\nNotifyEOSReached()\nNotifyBufferUnderflow(track)\nNotifyOutputProtectionRecovered()
NOT -> SCH : ScheduleAsyncTask
SCH -> CORE : SendErrorEvent() / NotifyEOSReached() /\nunderflow handling / mute + ScheduleRetune()

== Discontinuity (injector thread, synchronous) ==
INJ -> ARP : Discontinuity(mediaType)
alt PTS restamp active and no ES change
	ARP -> NOT : CompleteDiscontinuityDataDeliverForPTSRestamp(type)
	NOT -> CORE : direct call (no scheduler hop)
else EOS-based discontinuity and underflow monitor enabled
	ARP -> NOT : NotifyPipelinePausedToUnderflowMonitor()
	NOT -> CORE : mpStreamAbstractionAAMP->NotifyPipelinePausedToUnderflowMonitor()
end

== AV monitor ==
GL -> MAV : report timer tick
MAV -> NOT : SendMonitorAvEvent(status, positions, dropped)\n(same IStreamSinkNotifiable, not via the player)
NOT -> SCH : ScheduleAsyncTask
SCH -> CORE : SendMonitorAvEvent() -> MonitorAVStatusEvent

note over NOT, SCH
	Why the scheduler hop: a Rialto callback thread may hold a
	Rialto lock and then need an AAMP lock (mLock / mStreamLock)
	while an AAMP thread holds that lock and waits on a Rialto
	call: an AB/BA deadlock.  Deferring to the scheduler thread
	breaks the cycle.  The two discontinuity calls skip the hop
	because they run on AAMP's own injector thread.
end note

@enduml
